\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every nonzero real Banach space X with the ordinary approximation property, is X K-convex if and only if both X and its continuous dual have finite cotype, allowing different finite exponents for the two spaces?

